problem('dynamic-programming','climbing-stairs','Climbing Stairs','A robot climbs a staircase with n steps. In one move it can climb either one or two steps. Count the distinct ordered move sequences that reach exactly the top. There is one way to climb zero steps: make no moves.','easy','Dynamic Programming',['dynamic-programming','math'],[('n','int')],'int',[({'n':2},2,'The sequences are [1, 1] and [2].'),({'n':3},3,'The sequences are [1, 1, 1], [1, 2], and [2, 1].')],[({'n':0},1),({'n':1},1),({'n':10},89)],['0 ≤ n ≤ 45'])
